.bd
FUNCTION
.in +5
.br
strdup returns a pointer to a new copy of s, obtained with
malloc.  The copy belongs to the caller, who should return it
with free.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
RETURNS
.in +5
.br
the new copy of s.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
NOTES
.in +5
.br
strdup is a common extension rather than part of the original
C standard.
